 with the South African team Western Province on 10 March 2012 in a 51–22 victory over the Boland Cavaliers."},{"id":"34260630","n":"Ehren Painter","pos":"Prop","nat":"England","born":"1998-03-21","h":"1.93 m","w":"137 kg"},{"id":"34260658","n":"Elliot Young","pos":"Hooker","nat":"Scotland","born":"2004-03-14","h":"1.83 m","w":"105 kg"},{"id":"34161346","n":"Elvis Taione","pos":"Hooker","nat":"Tonga","born":"1983-05-25","h":"1.80 m (5 ft 11 in)","w":"112 kg (17 st 9 lb; 247 ","img":"https://r2.thesportsdb.com/images/media/player/thumb/ig3cam1581608436.jpg","bio":"Elvis Taione (born 25 May 1983 in Nukualofa, Tonga) is a rugby union footballer. His regular playing position is hooker. He previously played Super Rugby for the Western Force, Waratahs, Jersey in the RFU Championship and is currently signed to Exeter Chiefs, winning the Aviva Premiership in 2016/17. Exeter Chiefs signed Taione in March 2014 on a two-year contract."},{"id":"34260631","n":"Ethan Burger","pos":"Prop","nat":"South Africa","born":"2000-05-23","h":"1.92 m","w":"133 kg"},{"id":"34182074","n":"Ethan Roots","pos":"Back Row","nat":"New Zealand","born":"1997-10-11","h":"1.88 m (6 ft 2 in)","w":"110 kg (243 lb; 17 st 5 ","img":"https://r2.thesportsdb.com/images/media/player/thumb/dfuj2l1623463197.jpg","bio":"Ethan Roots (born 10 November 1997) is a professional rugby union player who plays as a flanker for Premiership Rugby club Exeter Chiefs. Born in New Zealand, he represents England at international level after qualifying on ancestry grounds. Early life Roots was born in Auckland to a Māori mother (Ngāti Kahungunu) and an English father from Reading."},{"id":"34260663","n":"Finn Worley-Brady","pos":"Back row","nat":"England","born":"2004-10-26","h":"1.88 m","w":"100 kg"},{"id":"34259876","n":"Franco Molina","pos":"Lock","nat":"Argentina","born":"1997-08-28","h":"1.98 m","w":"114 kg","img":"https://r2.thesportsdb.com/images/media/player/thumb/mjatnq1756825568.jpg"},{"id":"34260087","n":"Greg Fisilau